{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Like a House on Fire"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Work and Play"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le18ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reported speech (indirect speech) when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. <br/>In writing, it is common to use reported speech in storytelling and narrations. It allows the writer to share dialogue with the reader without always using quotation marks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past' since we are reporting the information at a later time. You need to change the verb to the next past form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> eaten.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\""}, {"type": "text", "content": "I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I</span></span> didn't want to go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">he</span></span> didn't want to go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: Where is the sun?<br/><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>: The wind asked <span class=\"strong\">where the sun was</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When the question is a yes/no questions, you use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> to report it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The sun asks <span class=\"strong\">if</span>/<span class=\"strong\">whether</span> the wind would be around without shifting temperatures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are mainly used in speech when we want to:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not</span>, or"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'<br/><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you</span>? <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</span><li> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"2\"> A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'<br/>  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you</span>?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</span> </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"italic\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same.<br/>For <span class=\"italic\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn'</span>t. Look at the examples in the chart."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is important, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are finished with that, aren't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You didn't go to work on Sunday afternoon, did you Peter? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You went downtown to another Bistro, didn't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You would like another, wouldn't you?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pitiful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "deserving or causing feelings of pity or sympathy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We always support you and your little pitiful problems with romance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when we are angry with someone."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hush"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make someone quiet, calm, or still"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why don't you hush and listen to me?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have your back"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "if somebody \"always has your back\" it means that they are always there to support you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We always have your back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make a scene"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make a public disturbance or excited emotional display"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are making a scene."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to scram"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "go abruptly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Get out of here! Scram! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hit the bricks "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sometimes insulting way of telling someone to go away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Scram! Peter. Hit the bricks! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Watch a TED TALK on a topic you find interesting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Watch it a couple times and take notes on the important information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the interactive transcript to select three important direct quotes from the TED Talk."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a brief summary of the talk and include the three direct quotes in your article as indirect speech."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I practice listening for gist and for detail."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes on my TED TALK topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I skim and scan for information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a brief summary of the talk."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about emotions, friendship and reaction in different situations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can quote other people."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Have you ever watched a TED TALK video? If yes, which one?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are your favorite TED TALK topics to watch?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "c